# Line-ending normalization. This file is the source of truth for line endings in this repo and
# overrides each developer's own Git config (notably Windows' common global core.autocrlf=true
# default), so every checkout gets LF regardless of OS or local Git settings.
#
# This matters most for bin/*: the dev Docker workflow bind-mounts the repo and execs bin/*
# scripts directly, so a CRLF shebang breaks with "env: 'ruby\r': No such file or directory".
#
# Only affects checkouts from this point forward. Anyone with an existing local clone needs a
# one-time `git add --renormalize .` (or a fresh clone) to fix their working tree — see README.md
# "Cross-platform line endings".

* text=auto eol=lf

# Explicit, even though `text=auto` above already covers these: bin/* has no file extension, and
# these are exactly the files that break the container shebang if CRLF slips through.
/bin/* text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf

# Rails encrypted credentials: a single line with no meaningful newlines. Never normalize it —
# corruption here means the file can no longer be decrypted.
*.enc binary

# Binary assets — none tracked today, but pinned so anyone who adds one doesn't need to remember.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
